Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:59:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] jailer: --new-pid-ns and --daemonize on macOS fork through
 the platform

macOS has no PID namespaces. The jailer takes Linux's path with a fork
in place of clone(CLONE_NEWPID): the pid file names the child, the
child leaves the jailer's session if the jailer led one, and the jailer
exits 0. What the namespace would hold is the jail's
(overlay/jailer/platform/macos new_pid_ns, vmm::ext::jail).

--daemonize's double fork is platform::daemonize on macOS: upstream's
steps, each fork made only while the jailer has one thread
(platform::fork_alone), since the child of each goes on as the whole
jailer. Linux's block is upstream's code, unchanged; the helpers only
it uses are built on Linux alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/jailer/src/env.rs | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

